{"step_index":1074,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:36:37Z","thinking":"**Revisiting Problem Formalization**\n\nThe problem involves a finite graph $G$ with certain properties: non-triviality, universal radius, and a total dominating set. The task is to prove a certain property, likely a theorem or lemma derived from these graph properties. Need to carefully re-examine the definitions of each given property, ensure correct formalization.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport random\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef bfs_dist(adj, n, start):\n    dist = [-1] * n\n    dist[start] = 0\n    q = deque([start])\n    while q:\n        u = q.popleft()\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if dist[v] == -1:\n                dist[v] = dist[u] + 1\n                q.append(v)\n    return dist\n\ndef test_all_tds(adj, n):\n    masks = [0] * n\n    for u in range(n):\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            masks[u] |= (1 << v)\n    target = (1 << n) - 1\n    eccs = [max(bfs_dist(adj, n, i)) for i in range(n)]\n    rad = min(eccs)\n    # Check all subsets s that are total dominating sets\n    for k in range(2, n + 1):\n        for s in combinations(range(n), k):\n            covered = 0\n            for u in s:\n                covered |= masks[u]\n            if covered == target:\n                # s is a total dominating set of size k\n                # Does there exist v in V with ecc(v) <= k?\n                # Since rad = min(eccs), rad <= k is EQUIVALENT to exists v with ecc(v) <= k!\n                if rad > k:\n                    print(f\"FAILED: n={n}, rad={rad}, k={k}\")\n                    return False\n    return True\n\nprint(\"Checking small graphs...\")\nfor n in range(3, 9):\n    for trial in range(50):\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        p = 0.3\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                if random.random() < p:\n                    adj[i].append(j)\n                    adj[j].append(i)\n        d0 = bfs_dist(adj, n, 0)\n        if any(x == -1 for x in d0):\n            continue\n        test_all_tds(adj, n)\nprint(\"All passed!\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing all total dominating sets","toolSummary":"Test all TDS for rad <= k"}}]}
